From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:29:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/112] Drive LPF: the bass compensation jumps with the
 ladder where the oversampling switches

The compensation's coefficients (k G^4, c) ramped from the last block's even where the ladder's own coefficients jump
(startBlock(): no last configuration, or the oversampling switched, which FilterSet crossfades). Across a switch the
last block's values belong to the other rate's G, so for one block the compensation did not match the loop it
compensates. Now it jumps with the ladder there. Steady output unchanged (tests/filters drive, filter_neutral static).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.cpp b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.cpp
index d62423ca..922717b1 100644
--- a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.cpp
@@ -244,6 +244,12 @@ void LpLadderFilter::renderDrive(q31_t* startSample, q31_t* endSample, int32_t s
 	if (frames <= 0) {
 		return;
 	}
+	if (!haveLast_ || lastOversampling_ != doOversampling) {
+		// Where the ladder's own coefficients jump (startBlock(): no last configuration, or the oversampling switched,
+		// which FilterSet crossfades), the compensation jumps with them: the last block's k G^4 and c belong to the
+		// other rate's G and don't match the loop they compensate
+		compLive_ = false;
+	}
 	if (!doOversampling) {
 		halfbandsLive_ = false;
 		driveCompensate(startSample, frames, stereo ? 2 : stride, stereo ? 2 : 1);
-- 
